This package (dsh-caveman) is an unofficial DeepSeek Harness port of
https://github.com/JuliusBrussee/caveman, pinned at commit
2e068f735253cce28256744804785f01887d9646 (upstream skill pack 2.2.0).

The files under skills/ are copied verbatim from the upstream repository at that
commit (the body of each SKILL.md). The upstream project is licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0; a copy of that license ships as LICENSE in this
package. Upstream keeps the pre-3.0.0 MIT notice in LICENSE-MIT for historical
contributions; nothing under skills/ in this package is drawn from the
engine/proxy/runtime code.

Modifications made by this port (Apache-2.0 §4(b) "state changes"):

- index.js: new file. Registers the upstream skill bodies with the DeepSeek
  Harness skill registry and APPENDS a "DSH runtime" section to each body at
  load time. The note states host facts the upstream text assumes differently:
  DSH has no caveman hook, so the active mode is conversational and is not
  stored anywhere; status answers must be marked "(not tracked by this host)";
  usage/savings are unmeasured on this host.
- package.json, cordis.patch.yml, README.md, test/, scripts/: new files; the DSH
  bundle layer, packaging, tests and installer. No upstream code.
- Not ported: the upstream CLI, proxy, engine, MCP server, Go runtime, hooks and
  the host-specific skills that depend on them (see package.json "caveman").

